From 8cb32d00ab3a088c6eaa126ab3202fb711c90391 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muse <muse@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:33:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] tun: add production packet-channel DeviceSource (Option
 B)

Promotes the FakeDevice pattern of crates/tun/src/testing.rs to a
production channel device (crates/tun/src/channel.rs), adds
DeviceSource::Channel and TunSource::channel (schema/api.json), a
PacketChannels registry in crates/api, Engine::start_channel_tun, and
the concord_packet_channel_open/write/read/close FFI. iOS feeds
packetFlow packets through the channel; no file descriptor is involved.

Rebased onto 5f1d090: upstream removed the TunSource::channel variant,
so this patch re-adds it (crates/proto/src/types/live.rs) and the
packet-channel arm in tun.start; Hub no longer holds a Control, so the
packet_channel_* methods go through self.server.service().
